# =============================================================================
# Store — LIST requests (VS Code REST Client) — GET /api/v1/stores (ADMIN)
# =============================================================================
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request below.
#
# Prerequisites: an admin persona (see http/store/create.http header for the
# SQL promotion one-liner).
#
# Notes:
#   - Run top-to-bottom on first use — later requests assume earlier ones ran.
#   - All data is FAKE. The automated suite: StoreApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Access tokens expire after 15 MINUTES. If tokened requests suddenly 401,
#     re-send request 1 (admin login) to refresh the chained tokens, then continue.
#   - Re-running: request 2's signup returns 409 — harmless, persona persists.
#   - Expected codes: 200 list (array, ALL statuses — filter client-side),
#     401 no/invalid token, 403 non-admin, 405 wrong method, 404 trailing slash.
# =============================================================================

@storeUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/stores
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: login the admin persona
# Expected: 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: signup a regular persona
# Expected: 201 (409 if she already exists — either way the account exists)
# @name regularSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bola Listless",
  "email": "bola.listless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234568"
}

### 3 — Setup: login the regular persona
# Expected: 200
# @name regularLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.listless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4 — List all stores as admin
# Expected: 200 — array of stores, every status included
GET {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5 — No Authorization header
# Expected: 401
GET {{storeUrl}}

### 6 — Garbage token
# Expected: 401
GET {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

### 7 — List as a regular user
# Expected: 403 — the collection is admin-only
GET {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{regularLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8 — Wrong method: DELETE against the collection
# Expected: 405 — Allow: GET, POST
DELETE {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9 — Wrong method: PUT against the collection
# Expected: 405 — Allow: GET, POST
PUT {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 10 — Trailing slash
# Expected: 404 — Spring 7 / Boot 4 does not do trailing-slash matching
GET {{storeUrl}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 11 — HEAD against the collection
# Expected: 200 — Spring auto-supports HEAD for GET routes (empty body)
HEAD {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
